WEBVTT

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:02.810
If the light touches me...

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:05.480
I'll die.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.670
What do you mean?

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:12.190
It's a disease from this island

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.030
called soot blight syndrome.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.410
"Soot blight syndrome"?

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.910
That's why I'm the princess of the night.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:31.010
It would make me happy to have a 
prince to join me in the night.

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:34.970
I'm going to bed.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.620
I was just waiting for you to wake up.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.300
Good night.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.990
<b>I don't want you to feel bad</b>

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:19.240
<b>Summer vacation reminders</b>

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:19.240
<b>Everything in moderation. When you go out,
 obey the rules and be considerate.</b>

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:20.690
Those continuing with school, 
keep your wits about you.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:25.000
Those who are job hunting, pay attention 
and don't get into any accidents.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.710
You have a handout with some helpful 
information, so read through them.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:28.710
<b>Ohara Family
Maid Wanted</b>

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:31.160
You've been told the same 
things since middle school,

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:32.840
so I expect that you know them.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.440
<b>You'll probably need a little money for living expenses.
 The amount for this month is half the usual.</b>

00:02:58.150 --> 00:02:59.700
Karen!

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:01.910
Let's do our summer homework together!

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:06.370
Let's aim for the impossible and try
to finish it all today at the shrine library!

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.290
Then we'll have all the 
rest of the time to play.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:09.260
Okay?

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:11.750
Sorry.

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:14.750
I have something to do today.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:27.640
Yeah! All done with my work for today!

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:35.400
I'm not even sure how to 
spell "soot blight syndrome."

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:46.660
Hey, you there!

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.010
This is the way to the library, right?

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:51.790
Y-Yeah.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.610
But it's closed.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:55.960
What? Closed?

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:59.850
Sara-chan... The director went up already.

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:01.820
How d'ya like that?

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:05.310
Never mind.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:07.380
Thank you, little girls.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.230
<b>Closed</b>

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:16.050
Of course.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:33.160
<b>Offerings</b>

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:36.580
Pyo!

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.140
"Pyo"?

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:39.960
B-But I'm glad you're here.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:44.880
I just finished praying to the gods 
for my honey trap to succeed.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:47.430
You're going about this the wrong way.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:52.680
Not to worry. I don't have 
much time, so I'm prepared.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:53.180
Huh?

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:57.120
Let's get going to my 
honey zone in the library.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.190
I'm just here to check something.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:03.810
Huh? That's the mayor, right?

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:06.070
This way.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.750
Hey, what's up?

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:15.410
He keeps telling me to come back.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:16.790
Come back?

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:21.020
Karen's family took me in a while ago.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.760
You mean they adopted you?

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.260
But they have a daughter.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:42.270
During the summer five years ago,

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:44.310
there was a fire in the main shrine building.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.950
We were surrounded by flames.

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:50.030
It was arson.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.330
When I woke up in the infirmary,

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:54.150
I heard my father and mother were dead

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:57.160
and only the shrine's object 
had survived the fire.

00:05:57.510 --> 00:05:58.920
That's awful.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:00.980
There are more than a few people

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:04.170
who do not think highly 
of the Garando family.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:07.960
Or any of the Three Families of Urashima.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:09.430
Meaning Rinne's family, too?

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:12.790
Also Karen's, the Kurutsu Family.

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:16.240
Our three families have histories 
dating back to time immemorial.

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:19.570
This island has legends about them.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.190
<b>Closed</b>

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:25.190
Long ago, there were three 
daughters on this island.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:30.570
Ohara Rinne, Kurutsu Karen, and Garando Sara.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:32.480
Those names...

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.410
Daughters born to the Three Families are

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:38.660
periodically given the names of 
the three girls in the legend.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.490
When this island was still 
connected to the mainland,

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:45.210
Rinne had an older brother named Setsuna.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:51.150
Unbeknownst to others, they began to 
love each other as a man and woman.

00:06:51.150 --> 00:06:53.680
Karen was the first to learn of it.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:57.450
But Karen, too, was in love with Setsuna.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:07:00.540
She scorned their immoral love

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:04.450
and asked the masked black shrine 
maiden to tear them apart.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:10.990
The black shrine maiden cursed 
Rinne, changing her into a monster.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:16.580
In despair, Rinne decided 
to take her own life.

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:21.560
Left alone, Setsuna accepted 
priestess Sara's advice,

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:24.550
and went to see the black shrine maiden 
who lived on a mysterious island,

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:26.000
making a pact with her.

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:30.760
At an unknown date in the future,
Rinne would be revived,

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:36.200
and if they met and were reunited, 
the curse would be lifted.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:42.160
Setsuna slept many years encased 
in ice, waiting for that day.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:45.280
In the unending flow of time,

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:52.820
Setsuna was given the name Sanzenkai, 
meaning the protector of the cosmos.

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:58.390
So... that's why she gave me that name.

00:07:58.390 --> 00:07:59.660
It would seem so.

00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:05.170
Two lovers waiting eternally for 
the day they'll be reunited.

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:06.840
<b>History of Urashima
Record of Island's Natural Disasters
Urashima Traditional Crafts
Urashima Town Government Chronology
Urashima Botanical Encyclopedia</b>

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:09.440
So, what about the actual Three Families?

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:12.840
They've continued to protect 
the island for generations.

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:17.290
Hey, do you have any books 
about soot blight syndrome?

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:18.460
Sure we do.

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:20.350
Try the local history section.

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:23.000
I didn't see that section.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:26.930
They're scattered around, 
so I'll pick some out.

00:08:26.930 --> 00:08:28.110
More importantly,

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.860
I'm ready, so let's do this.

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:36.700
Okay, Setsuna-san.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:38.580
Let's be a little more intimate.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:42.140
Hey, hold on! I told you you 
can't kill me with a honey trap!

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:43.670
That's not all.

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:46.550
After all kinds of investigation,

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:49.800
I'm thinking there may 
be another possibility.

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:52.170
Wh-What do you mean?

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:54.970
Do you want to know?

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:58.970
Hang on.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.940
About why you came from the future.

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:07.980
I'm getting closer to knowing 
the essence of why you exist.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:12.400
How can you know that when even I don't?

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:17.030
What if I said it's our destiny?

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:20.780
Please join me.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:24.440
No, not today.

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:26.040
Rinne will be waking up soon.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:27.450
See ya.

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:38.680
Thank goodness.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.680
I definitely wasn't ready.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:51.110
She has some strange delusions.

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:55.450
What am I so scared of?

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:05.790
What's with you?

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.790
Hey, what's with you?

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:10.460
I'm the maid in this house.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:12.540
Actually, I'm a guy, so maybe I'm the butler?

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:13.800
For real?

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:16.940
Then it was a waste of time.

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:19.760
I came here because of this.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:19.760
<b>Ohara Family
Maid Wanted</b>

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:22.660
Well, too bad.

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:24.870
This house doesn't need two maids.

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:26.880
I'll be the judge of that.

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:30.740
Hey!

00:10:31.350 --> 00:10:34.790
Staying out past dark without 
permission should get you fired.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:39.200
You've brought in a nice smell 
that's not from this house.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:40.970
Smell?

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:45.490
It's the incense Sara was burning 
when she set out her futon.

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:48.460
She did <i>what</i> when she set out her futon?!

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.700
Oh, nothing! Nothing! She did nothing!

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:52.140
Absolutely nothing at all!

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:54.380
Fired, fired, fired. And that's final.

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:56.500
Hang on, Rinne.

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:57.880
We didn't do anything, honest!

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.380
If you let me go, I still 
don't have my memory back,

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:03.390
so what can I do not knowing who I am?!

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:07.170
Never mind. I'll just go.

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:10.980
I'll decline, so please forgive him.

00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:14.160
Hey, what's gotten into you all of a sudden?

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:18.650
Even if I got the job, my dad 
would just drag me back anyway.

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:20.740
It's all a waste of time.

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:22.590
Sorry for stirring things up.

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:24.740
What are you talking about?

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:25.450
Come here!

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.160
Hey, what are you doing?!

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:28.550
Ow!

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:30.800
H-Hey...

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:33.170
Hold on, you two!

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:35.840
Get dressed in this!

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:38.420
Are you an idiot? What are you saying?

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:42.340
You're young, so don't go 
giving in to your parents!

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:45.970
If you lie to yourself and give 
up, you're bound to regret it!

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:50.980
What do you think you're talking about 
when you've lost your memory?!

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:52.050
I don't know.

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:54.770
I don't know, but...

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.710
that's what I think.

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:01.410
I just don't want anyone to have 
regrets, no matter who they may be.

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:12.520
Fine. I'll take you both on.

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:13.460
Really?

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.590
I don't want to have regrets, either.

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:18.090
Rinne...

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:23.060
Did you hear, Karen-chan?

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:23.590
Yeah.

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:25.580
That's great!

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:29.260
Why are you undressed?!

00:12:29.260 --> 00:12:31.570
You're the one who told me to change!

00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:36.740
Thanks, Rinne.

00:12:36.740 --> 00:12:37.730
For what?

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:40.120
For not firing me.

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:42.070
You really are such an idiot.

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:44.090
What?

00:12:45.390 --> 00:12:46.490
Never mind.

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:53.000
Where do I get off sounding so important?

00:12:54.840 --> 00:13:01.860
I don't even know what 
I'll regret and what I won't.

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:04.840
Why do I even exist?

00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:07.980
You don't need a reason for that.

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:09.930
You don't even need to think about it.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:16.930
Right now, I'm here, and you are next to me.

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:19.060
That's an indisputable truth.

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:23.190
You said your name is Setsuna.

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:25.840
You saw me and called me Rinne.

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:28.310
That's not a coincidence.

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:31.460
It's destiny.

00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:38.080
Then what was I trying to do with you?

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:41.260
You'll remember soon enough.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:45.310
You can take your time.

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:51.850
I'm here.

00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:54.220
What about school?

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:56.380
It's summer break.

00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:57.730
I see.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:59.130
You're...

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:00.480
What?

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:02.190
kind of cute.

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:08.210
What... Don't mess with me, you idiot!

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:09.160
Idiot!

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:12.910
I'm impressed you managed 
to shake off your dad.

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.850
I told him there was tutoring 
at the school and tricked him.

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:17.710
It's not a far-fetched lie.

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:18.830
I see.

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:21.750
I want to save one million by next spring.

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:24.340
Whoa, whoa, that won't happen.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:29.220
Don't interfere with my dream!
You're the one who told me to do it!

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:35.760
Maybe a million is a bit much.

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:37.770
What are you doing in the spring?

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:41.940
Graduating, obviously.

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:48.190
I'd like to drop out,
but my dad would give me hell.

00:14:48.190 --> 00:14:51.170
Would your mom not back you up?

00:14:51.170 --> 00:14:54.060
Mommy... My mother left.

00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:56.370
She left me and left the island.

00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:58.620
Sorry.

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:01.580
Don't be. It's been five years.

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:08.430
Hey.

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:09.470
What?

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:11.450
Can we stop someplace cooler?

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:13.560
Where would that be?

00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:15.220
I wouldn't know, would I?

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:17.260
Is that something to be proud of?

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:19.230
<b>Ice</b>

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:21.650
One melon ice and one with everything.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:24.420
Okay, they'll be right out.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:35.990
It's cooler than I expected.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:37.080
<b>Red bean soup</b>

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:37.080
<b>Tea house</b>

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:37.080
<b>Ice</b>

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:37.080
Yeah.

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:41.730
Are you planning to go see your mother?

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:44.900
You're going to tell me
there's no hope, aren't you?

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:46.090
I won't.

00:15:47.140 --> 00:15:49.140
Do you know where she is?

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:54.340
Starting from scratch will be pretty tough.

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:57.880
That's why I need the money.

00:15:57.880 --> 00:16:02.420
I'll get my own place on the mainland 
and use it to find mommy... my mother.

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:05.110
I want to change.

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:07.940
I'll treat you.

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:11.710
Not that it'll save you much.

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:13.830
Yeah, idiot.

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:17.830
Still, thanks.

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:25.000
Ma'am! Ma'am!

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:27.180
Medicine... My medicine...

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:28.140
Medicine?

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:30.920
Is this it?

00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:33.760
Hey, how do you read that?

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:35.550
<b>Soot blight syndrome
Pain relief</b>

00:16:34.230 --> 00:16:35.550
Soot blight syndrome.

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:40.560
<b>Morisu Clinic</b>

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:40.560
Hey, what is soot blight syndrome?

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:43.560
I heard that if sunlight 
touches you, you die.

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:46.280
In extreme cases, that can happen.

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:47.880
As soon as they're exposed to sunlight,

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:49.640
their whole body becomes inflamed.

00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:52.140
They could die in as little as five minutes.

00:16:52.140 --> 00:16:53.570
For real?

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:57.070
There's still no cure for it.

00:16:57.440 --> 00:17:00.580
All we can do is manage the symptoms.

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:08.080
You went on a secret date with Karen
when you have me?

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:10.700
We work together. That's all.

00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:11.530
More importantly...

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:14.150
I gathered some books 
on soot blight syndrome.

00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:16.830
Well, I don't need to know 
any more of the specifics.

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:19.760
I'm more concerned with whether the legend

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:21.760
and soot blight syndrome are somehow related.

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:23.520
Very perceptive.

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:28.730
<b>Soot Blight Syndrome
Endemic Diseases and Natural Medicine
Soot Blight Syndrome Medical Records
Asian Medicine</b>

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:28.730
This island was closed off from the outside 
world because of that endemic disease.

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:31.840
That's right. If soot blight 
syndrome didn't exist,

00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:34.800
there wouldn't be any such legend.

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:35.950
What do you mean?

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:41.480
The Kurutsu Family split the land, 
cutting off the island from the mainland.

00:17:41.480 --> 00:17:45.810
The Ohara Family split the sea, 
bringing its blessings to the island.

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:50.460
The Garando Family split the people's 
bodies, ridding them of disease.

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:54.700
Those stories were created by the great 
families of the three settlements

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:57.950
to fight back against persecution 
when the disease struck.

00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:02.850
When soot blight syndrome showed up 
in Rinne, the same as in the legend...

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:05.980
They're just using the legend to 
maintain their stupid authority!

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:09.730
No, the people needed help.

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:14.250
That's why the legend has 
survived for so long.

00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:16.090
It's to protect the island.

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:19.160
Who cares about this island? It's done for.

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:22.330
It's needed now precisely 
because it's nearly done for!

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:26.810
And that's why I've awoken?

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:32.090
And why I received the 
name Sanzenkai Setsuna.

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:32.840
Huh?

00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:37.340
Maybe it's a hint to recovering my memories.

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:40.590
Kuon, are you awake?

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.100
<b>Yes, wide awake</b>

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:46.740
This might be a rude question, but 
will you hear me out without getting mad?

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:50.670
Do you and Rinne have soot blight syndrome?

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:55.920
She does not.

00:18:55.920 --> 00:18:57.990
That's all I can say for sure.

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:02.660
I've told her several times, 
but she wouldn't listen.

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:04.300
So, why?

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:06.030
Why does Rinne act like that?

00:19:06.480 --> 00:19:09.190
She is intensely afraid of the disease.

00:19:10.130 --> 00:19:14.750
Is it connected to her disappearance 
and memory loss five years ago?

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:16.500
Yes.

00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:22.400
Having lost her memory, she began thinking 
of herself as the Rinne from the legend.

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:24.760
If nothing changes,

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:26.760
she'll continue to experience 
the curse forever.

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:29.140
Please save her.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:31.810
You...

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:34.130
You may be able to.

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:45.780
What do you think of Karen-chan?

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:48.910
She's a much harder worker than you, right?

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:49.870
Yeah.

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:51.280
If you don't keep on your toes,

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:54.040
she'll become the head maid 
and be in charge of you.

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:54.980
Yeah.

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:57.050
More importantly...

00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:01.670
Rinne, I'm not the Setsuna you think I am.

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:04.710
What's this, all of a sudden?

00:20:04.710 --> 00:20:08.000
And you aren't Rinne's reincarnation.

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:11.180
We need to stop this.

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:14.060
Pretending we're prince and princess.

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:25.490
Why? Why would you say that?

00:20:25.860 --> 00:20:27.860
Tell me, why?

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:30.490
Setsuna?

00:20:31.570 --> 00:20:33.840
Are you listening?

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:36.170
Sorry. What was the question?

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:37.960
Forget it.

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:39.300
Sorry.

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:42.740
I checked up on a few things.

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:47.550
That thing about not letting 
sunlight touch you.

00:20:47.550 --> 00:20:49.250
You should be fine.

00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:51.130
Did my mom tell you that?

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:51.600
Yeah.

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:57.920
So let's go to the beach some time.

00:20:58.350 --> 00:21:00.060
We're here now.

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:01.950
Not like this.

00:21:01.950 --> 00:21:03.360
During the day!

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:05.600
We can invite Karen and Sara.

00:21:05.600 --> 00:21:06.910
I'll pass.

00:21:07.520 --> 00:21:09.910
This is my destiny.

00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:14.420
Still, if you feel like it, 
you should come outside.

00:21:14.420 --> 00:21:15.420
It'll be fun.

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:16.420
I know!

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:20.920
But it's like you said!

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:24.340
You're Setsuna, and I'm Rinne!

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:28.430
Yeah, I said that.

00:21:29.590 --> 00:21:32.560
I don't know what it means, though.

00:21:34.340 --> 00:21:36.060
That's fine.

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:41.340
If I stay as I am, you'll 
always remain my Setsuna.

00:23:35.470 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>The right way to spin dreams</b>

00:23:36.450 --> 00:23:38.870
"The right way to spin dreams."
